  "next": {
    "tranche": "typed nominal mutation, capture, and callable-effect summaries",
    "why": "Unknown mutation-capable callable flow blocks both EventRecord and Sample and recurs for 48 constructed instantiations in 23 strict applications. The same missing effect fact also closed earlier caller-owned reuse work.",
    "entails": "Add a conservative fixed-point effect summary over functions, methods, and statically resolved lambdas; record nominal parameter field writes, capture or storage, return aliasing, unknown or dynamic calls, and propagate summaries through direct and monomorphic callable edges. Reuse the alias and conditional-retention guards, then rerun all 66 strict applications before considering any carrier change.",
    "importance": "This turns immutable-by-use from a benchmark observation into a typed compiler fact. It is prerequisite infrastructure for sound Go value carriers and other allocation removal while preserving Able reference identity."
